#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151941 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "150649f4-8b1e-563a-a774-1857d8781212" :question/math-academy-id "e-6247" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y$. This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151942 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "3923e1d8-73e5-501c-96b5-d6b729260d3a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6249" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) =10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 10-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[2,3].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152042 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/id #uuid "b3b3c2bc-029c-5128-8ea9-00591c6936d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-9496" :question/problem "Let $R = [2,3] \\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x - y + 3.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the lower Riemann sum $L(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $m_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x - y + 3$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})={x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1 \\leq i \\leq m$ and $1 \\leq j \\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}+3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3864f75-0cfa-59ee-a726-e7e8ad8d3439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565938} {:answer/id #uuid "cdbdc0e2-46d4-5cd9-88d6-e3a3f8868846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i}+3{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566012} {:answer/id #uuid "d738dade-ca06-5815-b4cf-c20bc75911a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j-1}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566025} {:answer/id #uuid "e64185c1-2e85-5ae8-b2eb-1ae0233f3132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+3{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566054} {:answer/id #uuid "f4ad7e6e-60bf-5f8b-97ed-47393ce42054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{x}_{i}-2{y}_{j-1}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3864f75-0cfa-59ee-a726-e7e8ad8d3439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565938} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dd5fb4c-de84-5f5b-af1b-04ba173b4cb6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00814162-4a3c-58fe-a969-f047df1ff44b" :question/math-academy-id "q-123512" :question/problem "Let $R=[4,5]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=8x-2y-1$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $8{x}_{i-1}-2{y}_{j}-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259532 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ede9bce-ae38-577e-bacc-87f020612226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j-1}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257197} {:answer/id #uuid "6500c138-a000-5c85-b486-9284962f6b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257668} {:answer/id #uuid "a76fe671-7d45-5709-aab4-68d346881651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258243} {:answer/id #uuid "afb8a0b8-c91b-53d8-92d2-f3dd9be2ef32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258312} {:answer/id #uuid "f02ab099-1461-5c8c-8a64-5841486261ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}+2{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afb8a0b8-c91b-53d8-92d2-f3dd9be2ef32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258312} :answer-field/id #uuid "f121ff54-6918-5739-ba1a-2bd0e425da2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e6e7588-d998-5d13-bde2-9f1ecbe236a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-123513" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5x-3y+20$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/a4/a44c2586978022663635d1f35399166c1ae32963fe0f4bffebd21966ad40bac5.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}_{(}f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j}+20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "afd97f63-933b-5595-8b4d-01f14c3bff53" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Function That's Neither Strictly Increasing Nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f75718e-b688-57f7-8da7-5b80fb085343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544190} {:answer/id #uuid "6468a315-f6fe-50ef-8ab8-9b9fb69c22ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544305} {:answer/id #uuid "a63af55b-729d-5110-9d15-e2d5527d8efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544445} {:answer/id #uuid "ab2fd54f-96ed-529e-86cd-ae8c068183d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544453} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5808ed-e840-541e-a0a8-45d1856fb2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i-1}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6468a315-f6fe-50ef-8ab8-9b9fb69c22ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544305} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e3b32ab-28f5-5977-974b-8d287db52031" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544693}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c350d5bc-4404-57ee-b54b-285bbf9a8f0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-123516" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [-2,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=y-2x+10.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-2x+10$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-2x+10$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/c4/c4aa9e96fe72a8fb31ab62ff7eb0695cc64992bb9433be516461915a5c92baff.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})={y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i}+10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88ab93c5-2e6f-5e91-a07a-8001a388875a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565894} {:answer/id #uuid "a4eb3739-cdd4-5966-bdce-45328695d2fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565943} {:answer/id #uuid "df46679a-b3ad-5fac-a8c0-89b76ac7c3cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}+{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566041} {:answer/id #uuid "e3b5c602-e4b2-58af-9e3d-48f821337d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566049} {:answer/id #uuid "e7651d5d-9a04-54e7-817f-50a0aa5721a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+{y}_{j}^{2}+2{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566056}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4eb3739-cdd4-5966-bdce-45328695d2fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565943} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f686c4b-9e7c-561e-8ea0-ed54cc445e3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f8d79c3-b613-54e6-b2e9-de270331920a" :question/math-academy-id "q-164124" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x.$ \nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,1]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+2x$ increases as $y$ increases on $[1,2].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{x}_{i-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475cfc3a-6171-510d-b62d-087df74508ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544244} {:answer/id #uuid "60822d5f-d7ea-5e7a-bddf-b9af1396fca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544297} {:answer/id #uuid "9dc118c3-8d11-514d-b55e-7e19aba8f614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544427} {:answer/id #uuid "b0dd0081-c931-5fa4-8e54-612dbedeec15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-2{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544460} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c13196-907f-5c49-b279-b3931cc9b82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60822d5f-d7ea-5e7a-bddf-b9af1396fca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544297} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe767b7b-e724-5de1-8c65-84a86b708adc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "086ea7e4-b45d-5b48-92bf-b7fd8532a3af" :question/math-academy-id "q-164125" :question/problem "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=16-2x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=16-2x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=16-2x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=16-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(16-{x}_{i}-{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $16-2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566250 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15287f6a-7570-5668-95d1-27e2083812d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-2{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565712} {:answer/id #uuid "27a5dea6-84d8-526d-9c28-419651f149c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160-{x}_{i}^{2}-2{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565741} {:answer/id #uuid "68c5de99-ca70-5eb2-9b6b-34ec81937577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i}^{2}-2{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565840} {:answer/id #uuid "ed036525-be4c-59cb-8765-6f9ccf606242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566066} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6ef2ea-2453-5bbc-8630-9a71d29f5017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-2{x}_{i}^{2}-2{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27a5dea6-84d8-526d-9c28-419651f149c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160-{x}_{i}^{2}-2{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565741} :answer-field/id #uuid "5424b5dc-8d67-5770-96ab-35a00ee79a30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e6c279a-ebea-5cc3-9684-5647027801a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-164126" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=160-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=160-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,2]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=160-{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[1,3].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=160-{x}_{i}^{2}-2{y}_{j}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(160-{x}_{i}^{2}-2{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $160-{x}_{i}^{2}-2{y}_{j}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39715562-cfd6-5124-85de-10923f2f02d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565771} {:answer/id #uuid "401993be-2c94-5901-a6c3-4b06e427b4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100-{x}_{i+1}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565785} {:answer/id #uuid "8405b19b-4be9-51fb-97b0-ea7d7a0ceb6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565885} {:answer/id #uuid "c71b3e38-9d3a-521c-8bb5-19963d524100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+5{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565998} {:answer/id #uuid "e88553cc-bcac-59c5-81de-b009be765660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+5{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39715562-cfd6-5124-85de-10923f2f02d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565771} :answer-field/id #uuid "a63d29ee-1939-56e6-932a-ce6d23d04a63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "579f4499-afd3-5e1e-813e-db4e394ec885" :question/math-academy-id "q-75063" :question/problem "Let $R=[1,5]\\times [2,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[1,5]$, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=100-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[2,7].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=100-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(100-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $100-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152718 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd33f89c-3adc-5b57-b7b7-4877a9e54e11" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a53e38-46ea-523d-a5e1-3ffcfcf1258e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565686} {:answer/id #uuid "586e1e12-4b69-5b7f-82ab-a83c9ddbe233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565825} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffd6892-9184-53c9-884c-ef1fd9595d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565831} {:answer/id #uuid "77f8de92-b6f2-5c9c-9dfd-cff3de94806a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565868} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ac1e00-9c17-5578-83d7-9b593f307fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "586e1e12-4b69-5b7f-82ab-a83c9ddbe233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565825} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0cc34b-e069-5efc-9a7e-61cc6ed50f8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186150815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1cb469e6-7b74-5371-89e3-14f53be7cb3a" :question/math-academy-id "q-75092" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=8-x-y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=8-x-y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=8-x-y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/4a/4a10c8332a5f346d393c37531c13db6aa69d4cecb241efd7c34d57f32d5a98b8.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=8-{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(8-{x}_{i}-{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $8-{x}_{i}-{y}_{j}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57764a62-5dc0-5a82-b628-694ac391cee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565822} {:answer/id #uuid "896ee499-3dea-5f95-aeca-c273d0b97faf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565898} {:answer/id #uuid "b672f322-9411-5602-9130-870b752e20c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565976} {:answer/id #uuid "cbeceaca-d3e1-5371-ad66-45ceae3d7944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j-1}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566009} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d2be4b-2c9e-563e-a447-219759f8e7ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2d2be4b-2c9e-563e-a447-219759f8e7ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566078} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed7fed9c-f180-5feb-9c85-76f5919b0235" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fe67796-b4b4-5e92-895d-48a77cf8ca60" :question/math-academy-id "q-75304" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x+4y+5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+4y+5$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+4y+5$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}+5)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}+5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02467f85-cb8c-52e6-8524-d58170a0e13a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544090} {:answer/id #uuid "02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544091} {:answer/id #uuid "a11f70f3-8e83-52f0-ae17-f28615c58f7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544436} {:answer/id #uuid "bf3f732b-b276-53da-8c54-4876b853e7d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544494} {:answer/id #uuid "f7c74500-e7ac-5eaa-beb4-4e1c203d88bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02b4f462-2c61-5567-8e86-726726c9ff96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544091} :answer-field/id #uuid "e449d4e6-5069-5c0a-ac4d-1bc5e9e548d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50a1adba-14a0-5a88-abaf-07e0387210e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-75306" :question/problem "Let $R=[3,4]\\times [-5,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x+y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $2{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45327c1c-8d20-5959-acce-f569c289c1cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j}^{2}+{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544238} {:answer/id #uuid "5171e819-ae3b-5116-9ea0-748dd049427a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}+5{y}_{j}^{2}+5{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544265} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a204c9-fc6a-55fa-a461-0281920bcca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544499} {:answer/id #uuid "db26df39-2212-562e-b5fd-592104bb0910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544560} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b31cd6-f6af-568c-89c7-ecabd44b45b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db26df39-2212-562e-b5fd-592104bb0910" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544560} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4f8ba87-584e-5b9c-b10e-58f5d8d221b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544727}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d148965-74db-5cec-9065-74d36d2d9d5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75307" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,2]\\times [1,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nL(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The lower Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{m}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ is the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $x$ increases on $[0,2],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+y$ increases as $y$ increases on $[1,5].$\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/51/51808df96cf7dd295bfa24aa3641a601c821116e1a0014898ffe705036704a53.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the lower Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{x}_{i-1}^{2}+2{y}_{j-1}^{2}+{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "41a9d47a-2dd6-5177-afd1-e4adcd887f55" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Lower Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac4729e-8c8c-50e9-af81-37849b7c020d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565693} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc4f999-4db4-5bd7-b7a9-6fd0df71be86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565849} {:answer/id #uuid "7acb1d76-417b-5aed-9993-7e382da4b0ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i}^{2}+7{y}_{j}^{2}-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565870} {:answer/id #uuid "878a3eb5-ad8a-5162-89a1-e11744ffc5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}^{2}+7{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565891} {:answer/id #uuid "c2aee6be-ca77-5900-9595-b950ed16105d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}^{2}+7{y}_{j}^{2}-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186565989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ac4729e-8c8c-50e9-af81-37849b7c020d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answe